  "article": {
    "id": "re-foundations-12b-how-will-we-live-in-2045",
    "title": "RE Foundations / 12B / How Will We Live in 2045?",
    "text_type": "informational",
    "audience": {
      "grade_band": "upper_elementary"
    },
    "language": "en"
  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Welcome to life in the future!"
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "You get up in the morning and look into the mirror."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "You’ve recently had a new anti-aging treatment, so you look like a 30-year-old."
          },
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "And many people your age could live to be 120 now, so—at 60—you’re not old at all."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "Science has also found amazing ways to keep people healthy."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "Nanotechnology 1 can help cure many illnesses, including cancer."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "And if any part of your body is unhealthy, you can “grow” a new one in a laboratory."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "As you get dressed, you say to your shirt, “Turn red.”"
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "It becomes red."
          },
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "In 2045, “smart” clothes contain nanoparticles that carry electricity."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "So you can program clothes to change colors or patterns."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "On the way to the kitchen, you want to call a friend."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "Your cell phone is by the window because it gets its energy from the sun."
          },
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "But you don’t need to pick up the phone."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "You can just touch your jacket sleeve to make the call."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "It’s breakfast time."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "You reach for the milk, but a voice says, “Don’t drink that!”"
          },
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Your fridge knows the milk is old, and tells the supermarket to replace it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "order": 6,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "As you leave for work, the lights turn off by themselves."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "Your home goes into “sleep” mode to save energy."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "In 2045, cars drive themselves, so you just tell your driverless car where you want to go."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "order": 7,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "Will all this come true?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "Perhaps the future is much closer than we think."
          },
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "1 Nanotechnology is the science of very small things that are measured in nanometers (one billionth of a meter)."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
